    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3bb61ce6-2f8d-52bf-8d8d-1be7b13256f8",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of $Ax=0$?\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A\\text{ is invertible}$\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\nSince $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0$, the nullspace contains a nonzero vector. Thus $A$ is not invertible. This does not determine its exact rank or nullity.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true: $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$. $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$.\n\n- Statement II is false: $A\\text{ is invertible}$. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false: $\\text{rank}(A)=4$. $\\text{rank}(A)<4$; the rank counts pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I only.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ce2bee8b-4b33-55f3-980c-ce98db5fc0b0",
